{
 "name": "VAOPGCPREC 73-90, Jul 18, 1990, Scope of 38 U.S.C. 360 [now 1160] in Relation to 38 U.S.C. 351 [now 1151]",
 "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center\">\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Decision Assessment Document<br />\tVAOPGCPREC 73-90,&nbsp;Jul 18, 1990, Scope of 38 U.S.C.&nbsp;360 [now 1160] in Relation to 38 U.S.C. 351 [now 1151]<br />\tOffice of General Counsel Precedent Opinion</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>What the opinion is about:</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Whether the provisions of 38 U.S.C.&nbsp;360 are applicable where a veteran's loss of use of an extremity is compensable under 38 U.S.C.&nbsp;351 and loss of use of the other paired extremity is neither service-connected nor quasi-service-connected under section 351.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">(This opinion, previously issued as General Counsel Opinion 11-87, dated October 2, 1987, is reissued as a Precedent Opinion pursuant to 38 C.F.R. 2.6(e)(9) and 14.507.)</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>Impact on VBA:</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Manual M21-1, IV.ii.2.G was revised in compliance with the precedent opinion.&nbsp; </span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>Summary of the facts and findings:</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">General Counsel held that section 351 eligibility confers entitlement to disability compensation provided under section 360, if eligibility otherwise exists.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">See OGC opinion for facts.</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>References:</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://www.va.gov/ogc/docs/1990/PREC_73-90.doc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.va.gov/ogc/docs/1990/PREC_73-90.doc</a></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a class=\"eGainArticleLink\" articleid=\"554400000014567\" articlename=\"M21-1, Part IV, Subpart ii, Chapter 2, Section G - Historical\" href=\"https://www.knowva.ebenefits.va.gov/system/ws/v11/ss/article/554400000014567?portalId=554400000001018&usertype=customer&\">M21-1, Part IV, Subpart ii, Chapter 2, Section G - Benefits Under 38 U.S.C. 1151</a></span></span></p>",
